/-!
# Dimension bound from an affine punctured local spectrum

Source: Stacks Project, Divisors, Tag 0BCR, `lemma-affine-punctured-spec`,
the only-if implication (blueprint: lem-sfb-affine-punctured-local-dimension).
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- An affine punctured spectrum of a Noetherian local ring forces dimension at most one.

Source: Stacks Project, Divisors, Tag 0BCR, `lemma-affine-punctured-spec`, converse.
(blueprint: lem-sfb-affine-punctured-local-dimension)

Proof:
1. Quotient by the nilradical. The quotient-spectrum homeomorphism preserves prime
   chains, hence dimension; the quotient remains Noetherian and local. Its puncture is
   the inverse image of the original affine puncture under a closed immersion and is
   affine. Use lem-weil-pbc-spec-quotient-homeomorphism-zero-locus,
   lem-weil-pbc-spec-quotient-closed-immersion and
   lem-weil-pbc-closed-immersion-affine-cover-criterion. We may assume A reduced;
   dimension zero already satisfies the conclusion.
2. Otherwise the maximal ideal is not minimal. Finite minimal primes and prime avoidance
   give f in the maximal ideal outside every minimal prime. Reducedness makes f a
   nonzerodivisor. Use lem-weil-pbc-noetherian-finitely-many-minimal-primes,
   lem-weil-pbc-prime-avoidance and lem-weil-pbc-reduced-zerodivisors-union-minimal-primes.
3. Write the affine puncture as Spec B, with restriction A → B. For g in the maximal
   ideal, the basic opens D_A(g) and D_B(g) agree, so their section rings A_g and B_g
   agree compatibly. Injectivity of A → A_f makes A → B injective. Multiplication by
   f on B is injective on stalks, hence on sections. Use lem-weil-pbc-basic-open-pullback,
   lem-weil-pbc-spec-module-tilde-sections, lem-pc-affine-localization-injective,
   lem-weil-pbc-affine-open-stalk-localization and lem-weil-pbc-localization-module-exact.
4. Put Q = B/A. Exact localization gives Q_g = 0 for every g in the maximal ideal,
   so each element is killed by some power of f. For a nonmaximal prime p, choose
   g in the maximal ideal outside p; then Q_p = 0, and likewise Q[f]_p = 0.
   Use lem-weil-pbc-localization-module-exact and def-weil-pbc-module-localization.
5. The connecting sequence is 0 → Q[f] → A/fA → B/fB → Q/fQ → 0. The first map sends
   b+A to fb+fA. It is well-defined and injective since f is regular on B; its image
   is the kernel of A/fA → B/fB. The last map sends b+fB to (b+A)+fQ; it is surjective,
   and subtracting fc from a representative proves exactness. Thus Q[f] is finite,
   by lem-weil-pbc-noetherian-submodule-finite. Its support is contained in the closed
   point, so lem-sc-generic-stalk-finite-length gives finite length when nonzero;
   the zero module has length zero.
6. Apply lem-sfb-power-torsion-cokernel-length: Q/fQ has finite length. By
   lem-weil-pbc-finite-length-module-simple-filtration it is finitely generated
   (simple factors are cyclic and generators lift through extensions). The connecting
   sequence then makes B/fB finite over A/fA, generated by 1 and lifts of these generators.
7. The finite map A/fA → B/fB induces a closed map of spectra, with image exactly
   the punctured spectrum of A/fA. Use lem-weil-pbc-spec-finite-ring-map-finite,
   lem-weil-pbc-finite-closed-map-finite-fibres and
   lem-weil-pbc-spec-quotient-homeomorphism-zero-locus. Every nonempty closed subset
   of a local spectrum contains its closed point. The puncture excludes that point,
   so it must be empty. Since f lies in the maximal ideal, A/fA is nonzero and has
   just its maximal prime; therefore its dimension is zero.
8. Dimension drop for the regular element f gives dim A = dim(A/fA) + 1 = 1, by
   lem-weil-pbc-dimension-quotient-nonzerodivisor. Include the dimension-zero case and
   the equality of dimensions before reduction to conclude dim A ≤ 1. -/
theorem ringKrullDim_le_one_of_isAffine_puncturedSpectrum
    (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A] [IsLocalRing A]
    (hP : IsAffine (puncturedSpectrum A).toScheme) : ringKrullDim A ≤ 1 := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry
